TURE (TOTAL OF LINES 800 TO 804)","form":"RS","row":"805","col":"1"}}]}],"context":[{"label":"Resident population","value":121416,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":3684000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":29745,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":33353,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2643.27,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":183.82,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Rushcliffe's 2025/26 outturn shows a council with no external borrowing at all: the Capital Financing Requirement closed at \u00a38.417m after a \u00a31.659m MRP charge, and the \u00a320m authorised borrowing limit / \u00a315m operational boundary were both unused all year, so the net-borrowing and CFR prudential indicators are reported as 'not applicable'. Financing costs to net revenue stream were negative, meaning investment income exceeded financing costs, and the council's own investment return of 4.33% beat its 4.06% budget, delivering a net return of \u00a32.05m against a \u00a31.43m budget. The one soft spot is the council's diversified (pooled) investment funds, which showed a \u00a30.749m fair-value deficit against initial cost at year-end, though this is cushioned by a \u00a31.31m reserve and a statutory accounting override (running to April 2029) that keeps any such loss out of the General Fund. The council's separate commercial Asset Investment Strategy property portfolio (\u00a316.1m original cost) returned an average 6.02% gross yield, similar to the prior year. Earmarked reserves grew to \u00a328.664m from \u00a324.289m the year before.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Outturn 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19459/Capital and Investment Strategy Outturn.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-06-18","signals":[{"code":"none","headline":"No external borrowing in 2025/26; \u00a320m authorised limit and \u00a315m operational boundary both unused; financing costs to net revenue negative (investment income exceeds financing costs)","why":"A council with no external debt and investment income comfortably covering financing costs carries very low near-term treasury risk; the reader should note only the modest \u00a30.749m pooled-fund fair-value deficit, which is reserve-backed and protected from the General Fund by a statutory override to April 2029."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr closing","value":"\u00a38.417m at 31/03/26 after MRP of \u00a31.659m (\u00a31.648m planned plus \u00a30.011m IFRS16 adjustment); no internal borrowing needed","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"authorised limit","value":"\u00a320m authorised limit for external debt set in the 2025/26 Strategy; indicator 'not applicable' as no external borrowing occurred","as_at":"2025/26 Strategy","page":4},{"name":"operational boundary","value":"\u00a315m operational boundary, set as an emergency precaution; unused","as_at":"2025/26 Strategy","page":4},{"name":"fixed variable rate exposure","value":"43% fixed rate / 57% variable rate exposure (Strategy limit is 50% fixed) \u2014 within limit","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":5},{"name":"principal sums over 1yr","value":"\u00a30 of investments held over 1 year against a \u00a336.299m limit (50% of total investment balance of \u00a372.598m; estimated limit had been \u00a336.5m)","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":6},{"name":"pooled fund holdings","value":"Fair value \u00a30.749m below initial investment cost at 31/03/26 (value had risen \u00a30.322m during the year); \u00a31.310m reserve held to mitigate losses; statutory override protecting the General Fund from any accounting loss runs to April 2029","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":8},{"name":"investment return","value":"4.33% actual return for 2025/26 (4.69% in 2024/25) vs 4.06% budgeted; net return \u00a32,051,880 vs \u00a31,434,900 budget","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":7},{"name":"financing costs to net revenue","value":"Negative (net investment income exceeded MRP and borrowing costs) \u2014 described qualitatively in the report; the underlying Table 4 percentage was not extractable as text from this PDF","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":5},{"name":"commercial portfolio","value":"Asset Investment Strategy property portfolio: \u00a316,137,154 total original investment value, average gross return 6.02% (6.06% in 2024/25); income \u00a3949,267 (2024/25: \u00a3952,764), decrease reflects reducing interest on the amortising Cricket Club loan","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":10},{"name":"earmarked reserves","value":"\u00a328.664m at year-end, up from \u00a324.289m in 2024/25","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":9},{"name":"esg holdings","value":"\u00a37.5m held in two ESG funds, 10.4% of total cash balances","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":6}],"commercial":{"pooled_fund_holdings":{"value":"Fair value \u00a30.749m below initial investment cost at 31/03/26 (value had risen \u00a30.322m during the year); \u00a31.310m reserve held to mitigate losses; statutory override protecting the General Fund from any accounting loss runs to April 2029","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":8,"doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Outturn 2025/26"},"commercial_portfolio":{"value":"Asset Investment Strategy property portfolio: \u00a316,137,154 total original investment value, average gross return 6.02% (6.06% in 2024/25); income \u00a3949,267 (2024/25: \u00a3952,764), decrease reflects reducing interest on the amortising Cricket Club loan","as_at":"2025/26 outturn","page":10,"doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Outturn 2025/26"}},"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"Financial Outturn 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19522/financial-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"14/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Designation of Local Nature Reserves",