racy.rushcliffe.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Rushcliffe clears audit with no significant weaknesses identified","lead":"Rushcliffe Borough Council has received an unqualified audit opinion from Forvis Mazars with no significant weaknesses identified in its financial sustainability, governance, or value-for-money arrangements. The council's 2025/26 accounts showed good quality and no issues arose from the audit, the Governance Scrutiny Group heard on 24 September. The council remains among the minority of authorities maintaining an up-to-date audit programme; many councils across England continue to receive delayed or qualified opinions. Auditors identified one uncorrected misstatement of \u00a3111k relating to property valuation indexation, treated as immaterial, but this does not affect the unqualified opinion. The audit conclusion has been delayed pending final assurance from the Nottinghamshire Pension Fund auditor but is expected well before the government's statutory deadline.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Annual Audit Letter and VFM Conclusion","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19767/19767.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Rushcliffe cleared by auditors with no significant weaknesses, despite control gaps exposed","lead":"Rushcliffe has received an unqualified audit opinion with no significant weaknesses identified in its financial sustainability, governance or value for money arrangements, putting it among a minority of councils that remain current with their audit programmes as many authorities across England struggle with delayed audits and qualified opinions. Forvis Mazars found no issues requiring recommendation. However, auditors did identify control failures during closure: a bank reconciliation error of \u00a31.823m was caught and corrected, and indexation errors worth \u00a3111k in the valuation of council property were left uncorrected as immaterial. The errors signal gaps in the council's first application of new accounting standards for five-yearly property revaluations. The council's pension liability of \u00a384.493m awaits final assurance from the Nottinghamshire Pension Fund auditor but no issues have been flagged.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Annual Audit Letter and VFM Conclusion","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19767/19767.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","paper_title":"Risk Management Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","headline":"New procurement compliance risk added for non-compliance with Procurement Regulations 2023","detail":"Risk identified that staff may be unaware of new procurement regulations, leading to non-compliant activity with potential financial penalties, legal challenge, and reputational damage. Rated as medium risk. Document notes BDO report identified much good work by council on procurement.","category":"governance","matters":"Procurement compliance failures can result in material financial penalties and legal challenges that directly affect council's finances","figures":"Medium risk rating","quote":"Risk that staff are unaware of new procurement regulations, leading to non\u2011compliant procurement activity, resulting in potential financial penalties, legal challenge and reputational damage.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","paper_title":"Risk Management Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","headline":"Inflation risk likelihood increased from 2 to 3, reflecting continued potential for price increases in 2026","detail":"Risk reflects potential for continued inflation affecting costs and budget volatility. Document notes this presents opportunity for higher investment income.","category":"other","matters":"Inflation directly affects council's cost management, budget forecast accuracy, and staff pay pressures; investment income from higher rates provides partial offset","figures":"Likelihood increased from 2 to 3","quote":"the likelihood has increased from 2 to 3 as there remains potential for increases to inflation in 2026. This also provides an opportunity with higher investment income.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","paper_title":"Risk Management Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","headline":"Government multi-year funding announcement removed central government funding uncertainty from risk register","detail":"Risk of one-year financial settlements preventing longer-term planning has been removed following multi-year funding announcement. This improves budget certainty and extends financial planning horizon.","category":"income","matters":"Multi-year funding certainty improves council's financial planning reliability, reduces forecasting uncertainty, and strengthens refinancing outlook","figures":"Risk removed from register","quote":"removed following financial uncertainty removed by muti-year funding announcement","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","paper_title":"Risk Management Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","headline":"New Financial Management System implementation due this financial year presents medium risk of delay or failure","detail":"Risk of delay or failure could result in poorly functioning system affecting statutory compliance, information production, supplier payments, with reputational damage and additional cost. External audit will examine controls once implemented.","category":"audit","matters":"System failures directly impact financial reporting accuracy, statutory compliance, and operational ability to manage supplier payments and cash flow","figures":"Due this financial year, medium risk rating","quote":"Risk of delay or failure in implementing the new system, resulting in a poorly functioning system that impacts statutory compliance, information production, supplier payments, and leads to reputa tional damage and additional financial cost.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Governance Scrutiny Group","paper_title":"Risk Management Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","headline":"Nottinghamshire councils including Rushcliffe entered period of uncertainty in July 2026 following Government LGR proposal, currently paused but assumed to resume","detail":"The proposal involves significant disaggregation for Rushcliffe. Implementation paused September 2026 but Government's preferred outcome assumed to continue. Council managing LGR risks through dedicated programme manager, LGR Board, Task and Finish Group, reserve fund, and key staff identification.","category":"governance","matters":"LGR is a fundamental change to council structure and governance; lenders must understand impact on financial stability, service continuity, and authority's capacity to service debt during restructuring","figures":"July 2026 announcement, September 2026 implementation pause","quote":"Whilst implementation of this decision has currently been paused (September 2026), the assumption is that this option continues to be the Government's preferred outcome and will, at some point in the future, be resumed.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Rushcliffe","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"New procurement compliance risk added for non-compliance with Procurement Regulations 2023","lead":"Procurement compliance failures can result in material financial penalties and legal challenges that directly affect council's finances","also":["40 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-10-13","n_findings":41,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Risk Management Update","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.rushcliffe.gov.uk/documents/s19773/19773.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":110,"news_drafts_total":2}}